No MIT option
-------------

These offer no MIT arm, so a saltator binary is distributed with at least
one of them under Apache-2.0 (or the named alternative). Apache-2.0 §4(d)
propagates any NOTICE file the upstream ships, which is part of why this
file exists.

    anyerror             Apache-2.0                    via openraft
    prost                Apache-2.0                    protobuf runtime
    prost-derive         Apache-2.0
    rocksdb              Apache-2.0                    the Rust binding
    sync_wrapper         Apache-2.0                    via tower/axum
    ryu                  Apache-2.0 OR BSL-1.0
    blake3               CC0-1.0 OR Apache-2.0 OR Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
    constant_time_eq     CC0-1.0 OR MIT-0 OR Apache-2.0
    moka                 (MIT OR Apache-2.0) AND Apache-2.0
    moxcms               BSD-3-Clause OR Apache-2.0
    pxfm                 BSD-3-Clause OR Apache-2.0


What is not covered here
------------------------

Build-time-only dependencies are excluded (`cargo tree -e normal`), because
they do not ship in the binary: `protoc-bin-vendored` and its per-platform
protoc binaries, `tonic-build`, `bindgen`, and the proc-macro crates'
build machinery. If saltator ever ships a source bundle rather than a
binary, that exclusion stops being safe.

The admin console's JavaScript dependencies are not in this file either.
They are built out of band (`npm run build` in `web/admin`) and embedded by
`saltator-admin-ui`; their notices belong with that bundle.
